Package: systemmonitor
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Homepage: https://github.com/epinephrinerx/SystemMonitor
Description: desktop widget for CPU, RAM, disk, GPU and network
 System Monitor is a native Linux desktop widget built with .NET and
 Avalonia. It shows CPU, memory, disk, GPU and network activity from the
 files the kernel and the drivers already publish, so nothing runs as root
 and nothing asks for administrator rights.
 .
 This package installs the program under /opt/systemmonitor and a menu
 entry. The program downloads and verifies later releases itself and hands
 the package to the desktop's installer; it never runs apt, dpkg or sudo.
